Content:
@here what do you think about having a large PTH as the pin1 marker. 
That allows someone to solder in a header pin into their motherboard that would force orientation. 
@RebelMike One thing about the circle in the wirebonding footprint is that it will likely be covered in black and you won't be able to see it anymore. ?Ideally? this sits far enough outside to stay clear of gunk (I made it much larger than it needs to be to account for process variabilities and things likely being done by hand)

@Leo Moser (mole99) - I think the wafer.space logo being mandatory when doing wafer.space CoB bonding is probably something we want to do? (For people doing bare die, they can do whatever they want....)

I'm ***pretty*** sure the idea was that diagonal corners to **never** be the same (filled verse unfilled) so it didn't matter if you could actually understand/recognize the graphics -- you just needed to determine "is there something there or not".

Am I mistaken?
